packaging (minimum)	Prepare toolchain image	2026-10-12T11:01:35.3475830Z             "body": "Integrate iteration 029 Arch packaging into the protected main workflow. Future stable releases build an exact-commit, pacman-owned shared package using system Qt and paths; upload requires verified Ubuntu and Arch archive/checksum pairs and refuses differing published bytes. Existing v1.1.0 assets, versions and renderer behavior stay unchanged.\n\nLocal verification: 40 Python tests passed, Bash syntax and release workflow gates passed, documentation links and historical evidence/helper hashes validated. Historical logs remain byte-identical.\n\nBefore merge, require both packaging checks and the complete manual release workflow on this exact PR revision: Ubuntu shared/static/CommonMark/lint/consumers/benchmark, minimum-built binary lifecycle on both Qt runtimes, Arch metadata/payload/namcap/fresh pacman integrity/four consumers/temporary upgrade/removal, with upload skipped. Repeat all gates on the exact main merge commit and retain final evidence separately.\n\nArch uses current rolling repositories; each run records image/package identities and provenance rather than promising reproducible hashes. No release publication, asset upload, host package installation, AUR or protection changes.\n",
